# Command: MC (Read, Set and Answer frames)
# Radio: Kenwood TS-480HX / TS-480SAT
# Title (cover, verbatim): "PC CONTROL COMMAND REFERENCE FOR THE TS-480HX/ SAT
#   TRANSCEIVER"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries "KENWOOD CORPORATION",
#   "(c) 2003/11/28" and the printing code line "09 08 07 06 05 04 03 02 01 00".
# Source page: printed folio "12"  ==  PDF page 13 of 26
# Charts used: the Set, Read and Answer charts of the MC block
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler):
#   MC Set    = 6 positions
#   MC Read   = 3 positions
#   MC Answer = 6 positions
#   (identical to the TS-590 book's MC lengths)
#
# CHARTS, position by position:
#   Set:     1 M  2 C  3 P1  4 P2  5 P2  6 ;      (7..10 empty)
#   Read:    1 M  2 C  3 ;                        (4..10 empty)
#   Answer:  1 M  2 C  3 P1  4 P2  5 P2  6 ;      (7..10 empty)
#
# Field map:
#   pos 1-2  "MC"
#   pos 3    P1  (1 character)
#   pos 4-5  P2  (2 characters)
#   pos 6    ";"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANNEL-NUMBER LEGEND, VERBATIM (the complete right-hand column; block description
# reads "Recalls or reads the Memory channel."):
#
#   Parameters:
#   P1
#     0: Always 0 for the TS-480 (Memory bank number).
#   P2
#     00 ~ 99: Channel number
#
#   THAT IS THE WHOLE LEGEND.  This book prints NO P-channel wording and NO
#   extension-channel wording for MC - no "P00 ~ P09", no "E00 ~ E09", no 100~119
#   mapping.  The only channel-range wording anywhere near it is elsewhere in the
#   book and is quoted here so the absence is on the record:
#     MR / MW (folio 13-14) VERBATIM: "Memory channel 90 ~ 99: / P1=0 (start
#       frequency), P1=1 (end frequency)"
#     SS (folio 20 / PDF p.21) VERBATIM: "0 ~ 9: Memory Channel number for the Program
#       Scan / (0: Memory Channel 90 ~ 9: Memory channel 99)"
#
# EVERY POSITION THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always" (by position number):
#   position 3 (P1) -- "0: Always 0 for the TS-480 (Memory bank number)."
#   (The TS-590 book's MC has NO fixed position at all - see FINDING F8.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   [C1] The particular channel numbers below are ASSUMED illustrative values.
#   Every byte's WIDTH and every fixed byte's VALUE is documented.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim)
#
mc480_read	MC;
mc480_set_ch00	MC000;
mc480_set_ch03	MC003;
mc480_set_ch90_program_scan_lower	MC090;
mc480_set_ch99_top_of_range	MC099;
mc480_answer_ch03	MC003;
mc480_answer_ch99	MC099;
